      "description": "Social Work Lecturer Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're on our Australia website Change Region United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Canada Canada (Fr) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides CV Templates Interview Prep Career Guides Employee Stories Support Centre All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Hiring & Recruitment Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Leadership Excellence Employee Experience Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Effective 1:1s Mentorship Trending Topics All Topics Get Started Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resources Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre All Resources topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Productivity & Innovation Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Social Work Lecturer Social Work Lecturer at Excelsia University College School of Social Work • Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Hold a qualifying Social Work degree with eligibility for membership with AASW (essential). Experience teaching in higher education at tertiary level, including curriculum development/modification. Frontline experience in complex service environments (e.g., hospital settings or DCJ). Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Qualified Description Permanent, full-time position Remuneration commensurate with Academic level. Be a part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community! About the role Ensuring the activities of the School are operated effectively and providing a quality service to the students and staff. Lecturing in agreed subject areas and managing teaching and assessment of units being delivered. Producing research and/or scholarship that informs learning and teaching, and curriculum innovation and development. Providing administrative support to the Head of School and other academic staff. Provision of field education liaison duties to students undertaking their practicum placement and experience. Contribute to course and unit coordination duties and program development and curriculum design. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Hold a PhD qualification in relevant discipline (desirable). Hold a qualifying Social Work degree with eligibility for membership with AASW (essential). A background in Higher Education spanning experience teaching at a tertiary level and including curriculum development and modification and/or a background in fieldwork, spanning frontline experience in a complex service environment, e.g. hospital settings or the Department of Communities and Justice (DCJ). Essential: Ability to teach and model practical, real-world skills to students and early-career professionals Ability to communicate and work effectively and cooperatively with staff and students. An understanding of current and emerging trends in Social Work Education and training. Technological literacy and experience in online education and communication platforms. Demonstrated awareness of, and sensitivity to, diversity with the ability to work with students, staff, and administrators, including pastoral skills in mentoring staff and supporting students. Committed Christian, involved in a local congregation. Full Australian working rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy flexible and family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a culturally rich environment, with opportunities to engage in spiritual devotions. Upskill with our substantial College tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families. Our employees have access to early wage access that offers instant access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education and much more. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the Employment Hero Group by email, text, and social media channels about its services and activities. You may withdraw your consent at any time. See the Privacy Policy for information on how your data is processed. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians 