    "https://employmenthero.com/jobs/position/excelsia-university-college-research-grant-officer-uxbk1/": {
      "title": "Research Grant Officer",
      "description": "Research Grant Officer Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're on our Australia website Change Region United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Canada Canada (Fr) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides CV Templates Interview Prep Career Guides Employee Stories Support Centre All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Hiring & Recruitment Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Leadership Excellence Employee Experience Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Effective 1:1s Mentorship Trending Topics All Topics Get Started Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resources Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre All Resources topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Productivity & Innovation Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Research Grant Officer Research Grant Officer at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary 2+ years demonstrated experience in research administration, grant writing, or post-award contract management in an AUun Strong understanding of pre-award and post-award processes across the full grant lifecycle. Must have full Australian Working Rights. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Experienced Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to play a pivotal role in securing and managing research funding that advances innovation, scholarship, and institutional impact. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role The Grants Officer delivers high-quality administrative, financial, and strategic support across the full research grant lifecycle. The role strengthens the competitiveness of applications to major funding schemes – including government, industry, and community grants – while ensuring strict adherence to Excelsia University College policies, budget structures, and legal compliance frameworks. Primary responsibilities include: Strengthen research funding capability by promoting and supporting access to external funding opportunities. Provide strategic, high-level advice that strengthens the competitiveness and quality of grant applications. Maintain effective research administration systems and submission processes. Deliver accurate and strategically aligned budgets that maximise cost recovery and sustainability. Ensure successful grants are established and administered effectively. Ensure research funding is administered in accordance with ethical, legal and institutional requirements. Maintain accurate, reliable, and timely grant data to support institutional reporting and strategic decision-making. Act as a trusted advisor and central point of expertise in research grant administration. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Possession of relevant tertiary qualification in research administration, business, finance, or a related field, or equivalent demonstrated experience. Demonstrated experience in research administration, grant writing, or post-award contract management within an Australian university setting. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent) would be an advantage. An understanding of current and emerging trends in higher education. Strong understanding of the grant lifecycle, including pre-award and post-award processes. Proven ability to interpret and apply complex external funding guidelines and legislative frameworks. Strong competency in constructing, reviewing, and reconciling complex research budgets, financial declarations, and institutional on-costs. Proficiency using institutional research management systems (e.g. Esploro, or equivalent platforms such as Pure or ResearchMaster), alongside federal funding portals such as RMS Technological literacy in a wide range of desktop applications to support reporting and analysis role requirements. Highly developed interpersonal and written communication skills, with a proven track record of guiding and negotiating with busy academic staff. Strong attention to detail in preparing documents, reports, and records. Excellent oral and written communication skills, and confidence in presentations. Exceptional organisational skills, with the ability to manage high-pressure workloads and competing deadlines during peak major grant rounds. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education, and much more. This full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for fol