development activities. Coordinate the planning, delivery and continuous improvement of conferences, forums, workshops and sector engagement events to provide a high-quality experience for members and stakeholders. Provide administrative coordination for quality initiatives, publications and strategic projects as directed by the Provost. Provide high-level administrative support to activities and foster effective stakeholder relationships. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Diploma or Bachelor’s degree in Event Management, Marketing, Communications, Business Administration, Public Relations or a related discipline; or an equivalent combination of relevant qualifications and demonstrated experience. Demonstrated experience coordinating conferences, events or professional development activities. Experience providing high-level administrative support in a complex organisational environment, managing multiple priorities and coordinating projects to meet deadlines. Experience building and maintaining effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Experience using event management systems, website content management systems or online collaboration platforms. Experience in the higher education, education, not-for-profit or membership association sector is desirable. Ability to work independently, exercise initiative and contribute effectively as part of a team. Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to adapt to changing priorities. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through