      "description": "Campus Coordinator Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're on our Australia website Change Region United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Canada Canada (Fr) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides CV Templates Interview Prep Career Guides Employee Stories Support Centre All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Hiring & Recruitment Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Leadership Excellence Employee Experience Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Effective 1:1s Mentorship Trending Topics All Topics Get Started Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resources Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre All Resources topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Productivity & Innovation Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Campus Coordinator Campus Coordinator at Excelsia University College Facilities • Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Possession of a relevant qualification or equivalent combination of experience/training. Prioritise tasks and meet deadlines for daily maintenance and event setup. Good communication to interact effectively with staff and contractors. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Experienced Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking & close to public transport. A fantastic opportunity to perform a variety of tasks to maintain the cleanliness,\nfunctionality, and safety of Excelsia. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: Coordinate sound daily maintenance operations of the campus. Inspect building facilities to identify building maintenance needs and any safety concerns. Actively participate in the positive development of campus facilities and maintenance of\nclassrooms and equipment. Engage in campus walk throughs of student and common spaces to ensure readiness of daily\nactivities. Ensure adequate stock levels of office supplies. Provide support to set up for Excelsia events. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Possession of a relevant qualification, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience/ training. Essential: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Prior working experience with transferrable skills. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent) would be an advantage. Proven organisational skills with the ability to prioritise and meet deadlines. Demonstrated high attention to detail and commitment to maintaining high standards of safety\nand cleanliness. Good communication skills to interact with staff and contractors. Basic understanding of building maintenance and repair procedures. Technologicalliteracy in a range of desktop applications to support administrative elements\nof role. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy flexible and family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a culturally rich environment, with opportunities to engage in spiritual devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education and much more. Learn more about why Excelsia is Great Place to Work ® Certified and why our staff love working at\nExcelsia here: https://greatplacetowork.com.au/companies/excelsia-college/ How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria\nvia this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us at work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the Employment Hero Group by email, text, and social media channels about its services and activities. You may withdraw your consent at any time. See the Privacy Policy for information on how your data is processed. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the lands where we live, learn and work. © 2026 Employment Hero Pty Ltd. All rights reserved. Trust & Legal Centre Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Data Processing Addendum Cookie Policy Financial Disclosure Documents Close Clear Showing 0 results of 0 for \" \" Top Results Businesses (0) Partners (0) Employees (0) Job Seekers (0) Resources (0) Company About us