      "description": "Student Placements Coordinator Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're on our Australia website Change Region United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Canada Canada (Fr) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides CV Templates Interview Prep Career Guides Employee Stories Support Centre All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Hiring & Recruitment Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Leadership Excellence Employee Experience Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Effective 1:1s Mentorship Trending Topics All Topics Get Started Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resources Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre All Resources topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Productivity & Innovation Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Student Placements Coordinator Student Placements Coordinator at Excelsia University College Student Placements • Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Experience in networking and stakeholder relationship management with industry representatives. Demonstrable account/relationship management and/or business development for placements in Social Work and Community Ser Proven organisational skills to prioritise work and meet deadlines. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Mid-level Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to source placements for Social Work and Community Services students through networking and industry visits. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. Due to continued growth at Excelsia University College, we are expanding our student placements team and are seeking additional team members to join us during this exciting period of growth. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: To provide support to the Director of Student Placements and Field Education Coordinators. To build and nurture industry relationships to develop and maintain potential placement partners for Social Work and Community Services placement units. To research, identify, and initiate new opportunities to attract and establish long-term and mutually beneficial partnerships. To triage, review, and assess new leads to refer to Field Education Coordinators to qualify in line with relevant accreditation bodies to become placement partners. To support associated relationship building and partner onboarding. To collaborate to identify and formalise a suitable number of placement partners to cater to each cohort of placement students. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Possession of a degree level qualification or relevant combination of experience and training, in a relevant field such as Sales, Marketing, or Business Administration, and/or Social Work or Community Services. Essential: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Experience in networking, stakeholder relationship management and engagement with industry representatives. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent) would be an advantage. Proven organisational skills with the ability to prioritise and meet deadlines. Demonstrable experience in account, relationship management and/or business development (in required areas, or higher education, other relevant industry as examples) Excellent communication/ interpersonal skills and ability to build rapport with a wide variety of stakeholders. Outcomes focused and comfortable working in a target driven environment. Able to work both independently and as part of a collaborative team to achieve required outcomes. Disciplined with record keeping and confident/experienced in managing data and using a variety of technology (InPlace, CRM, highly desirable) Persistent, solutions- focused and agile, with the ability to effectively manage conflicting priorities, timelines and demands. Strong presentation skills and ability to adapt communication style to suit diverse networks. Ability to collaborate and negotiate with both internal and external stakeholders to positively influence and deliver mutually beneficial outcomes. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy flexible and family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a culturally rich environment, with opportunities to engage in spiritual devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education and much more. Learn more about why Excelsia is Great Place to Work ® Certified and why our staff love working at Excelsia here: https://greatplacetowork.com.au/gptwcertified/excelsia-college/ This on-site, full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT 