      "description": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer – Education (Early Childhood) – PHD Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're on our Australia website Change Region United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia New Zealand Canada Canada (Fr) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides CV Templates Interview Prep Career Guides Employee Stories Support Centre All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Hiring & Recruitment Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Leadership Excellence Employee Experience Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Effective 1:1s Mentorship Trending Topics All Topics Get Started Trending Article How to ace AI virtual interviews with Employment Hero’s Recruitment Agent 5 min read Article What is the hidden job market? 9 min read Article What is career cushioning? 7 min read Article Top employee benefits in 2025 6 min read Article The history of the cover letter (and its future) 5 min read Resources Webinars & Events Video & Audio Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre All Resources topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Productivity & Innovation Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer – Education (Early Childhood) – PHD Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer – Education (Early Childhood) – PHD at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Hold a PhD in Early Childhood Education or be currently undertaking a PhD in Early Childhood Education. Demonstrated experience in teaching at a tertiary level, learning, scholarship and research. Demonstrated ability to teach online and face to face, with excellent communication skills. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Qualified Description Full-time position Pennant Hills campus Lecturer Level B / Senior Lecturer Level C Be a part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community About the Role Primary responsibilities include: Teaching and unit coordination in agreed subject areas including managing and assessment of the units. Providing a quality education, care and support to the students. Ensuring the activities of the School are operated effectively and efficiently, Producing research and scholarship that informs learning and teaching, and curriculum innovation and development. Providing administrative support to the Head of School, Course Coordinators, and other academic staff. Building the profile and reputation of Excelsia with stakeholders, the community and potential students. Essential Criteria: Committed Christian, involved in a local congregation. Hold a PhD in Early Childhood Education or be currently undertaking a PhD in Early Childhood Education. Teaching experience and ECT qualification would be an advantage. Demonstrated experience in teaching at a tertiary level, learning, scholarship and research. Teaching experience in Early Childhood sector would be an advantage. Demonstrated expertise in ECEC and understanding of current and emerging trends in Australian Education. Excellent communication skills. Demonstrated ability to teach online and face to face. Awareness of and sensitivity to cultural diversity and ability to work with students, staff, and administrators cooperatively. Full Australian Working Rights. WWCC About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian Arts College. We are now a  part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your income with Salary Packaging scheme. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Enjoy our modern campus in Pennant Hills. Walk 5 minutes from transport or park onsite for free. Work in Great Place to Work ® Certified organisation How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community at Excelsia University College. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Early applications are encouraged. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the Employment Hero Group by email, text, and social media channels about its services and activities. You may withdraw your consent at any time. See the Privacy Policy for information on how your data is processed. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the lands where we live, learn and work. © 2026 Employment Hero Pty Ltd. All rights reserved. Trust & Legal Centre Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Data Processing Addendum Cookie Policy Financial Disclosure Documents Close Clear Showing 0 results of 0 for \" \" Top Results Businesses (0) Partners (0) Employees (0) Job Seekers (0) Resources (0) Company About us Careers Become a partner Media Centre Get in Touch Contact Us Sales HR Login Support Service Centre Help Centre Implementation Hub Pick your 