mote Working Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Productivity & Innovation Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Casual Social Work and Counselling Lecturers Casual Social Work and Counselling Lecturers at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Casual AI Job Summary Hold a PhD, Masters, or postgraduate qualification in Social Work or Counselling. Lecturing/teaching experience (3+ years is an advantage). Be eligible for membership with AASW or ACA and/or PACFA. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Temporary • Casual • Qualified Description Casual opportunities commencing February 2026 Free onsite parking and close to public transport Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: Tutoring in agreed subject areas and managing teaching and assessment of units being delivered. Participating in the administration, assessment, and examination of students. Contributing to scholarship activities in Social Work and/or Counselling courses. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Hold a PhD, Masters, or postgraduate qualification in relevant Social Work or Counselling discipline. Lecturing and teaching experience (3+ years experience would be an advantage). Essential: An understanding of current and emerging trends in Social Work or Counselling. Ability to communicate effectively with students; ability to communicate and work effectively and cooperatively with colleagues. Technological literacy and experience in developing online communication tools and previous experience in online education is desirable. Demonstrated awareness of and sensitivity to diversity and ability to work with students, staff, and administrators, including pastoral skills in mentoring staff and supporting students. Be eligible for membership with AASW or ACA and /or PACFA These casual positions are based in Pennant Hills. Learn more about why Excelsia is Great Place to Work ® Certified and why our staff love working at Excelsia here: https://greatplacetowork.com.au/companies/excelsia-college/ How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Int